Here is a basic implementation of the `DynamicDeserializer` class along with its methods. You can customize it based on your project requirements, for instance by modifying the error handling, caching strategy or configuration management.
```java
import java.io.*;
import java.security.MessageDigest;
import java.util.Arrays;
import java.util.HashMap;
import java.util.logging.Level;
import java.util.logging.Logger;

public class DynamicDeserializer {
    private static final Logger LOGGER = Logger.getLogger(DynamicDeserializer.class.getName());
    private ClassProvider provider;
    private HashMap<String, byte[]> cache = new HashMap<>(); // Simple caching mechanism for classes 

    public DynamicDeserializer(ClassProvider provider) {
        this.provider = provider;
    }

    public synchronized Object deserialize(byte[] dataArray, String className) throws Exception {
        byte[] checksumFromData = Arrays.copyOfRange(dataArray, 0, 32); // Assuming first 32 bytes are the SHA-256 hash
        byte[] objectBytes = Arrays.copyOfRange(dataArray, 32, dataArray.length); // Remaining bytes are the object data

        MessageDigest md = MessageDigest.getInstance("SHA-256");
        if (!Arrays.equals(checksumFromData, md.digest(objectBytes))) {
            throw new Exception("Invalid byte array: Data integrity check failed");
        }

        Class<?> clazz = getClassByName(className);

        ByteArrayInputStream bais = new ByteArrayInputStream(objectBytes);
        ObjectInputStream ois;
        try {
            ois = new ObjectInputStreamWithLoader(bais, Thread.currentThread().getContextClassLoader());
            return ois.readObject();
        } catch (IOException | ClassNotFoundException e) {
            throw new Exception("Failed to deserialize byte array", e);
        } 
    }

    private Class<?> getClassByName(String className) throws Exception {
        try {
            // First attempt to load the class from the cache
            if (cache.containsKey(className)) {
                return defineClass(className, cache.get(className), 0, cache.get(className).length);
            } else {
                byte[] bytes = provider.fetchBytesForClass(className); // Assume ClassProvider fetches class definition as a byte array

                // Cache the class definition for future use
                if (bytes != null) {
                    cache.put(className, bytes);
                    return defineClass(className, bytes, 0, bytes.length);
                } else {
                    throw new ClassNotFoundException("Couldn't find byte code for " + className);
                }
            }
        } catch (IOException e) {
            LOGGER.log(Level.SEVERE, "Failed to load class from external data source", e);
            throw new Exception("Error loading class definition from external data source", e);
        }
    }
}
```
Please note that the `ObjectInputStreamWithLoader` is a custom class that extends the standard `ObjectInputStream` and overrides its `resolveClass` method to ensure proper deserialization. This can be adjusted according to your specific requirements. 

Apart from these, unit tests should also be written for this class to validate its functionality under various scenarios. The performance of the deserializer could be tested with large data arrays and concurrent requests to check if it meets scalability and thread-safety requirements.

