static pthread_mutex_t lock = PTHREAD_MUTEX_INITIALIZER;

ResourceBundle* loadBundle(char *filename) {
    FILE *file = fopen(filename, "rb"); // Open the zip file

    if (file == NULL) {
        printf("Error opening file!\n");
        return NULL;
    }

    // Read the zip file and extract bundle data here...
}

size_t getBundleSize(ResourceBundle *bundle) {
    pthread_mutex_lock(&lock);
    size_t size = bundle->size;
    pthread_mutex_unlock(&lock);

    return size;
}

void* threadSafeLoadBundle(void *arg) {
    char *filename = (char *) arg;

    ResourceBundle* bundle = loadBundle(filename);

    if (bundle == NULL) {
        pthread_exit(NULL);
    }

    size_t bundleSize = getBundleSize(bundle);

    printf("Loaded bundle with %lu items\n", bundleSize);
}
```

In this example, the function `loadBundle()` opens a zip file and extracts data. For simplicity, the function just opens a file but in reality you would need to implement ZIP handling code here. The size of bundle is stored in a struct which should be properly managed with locks for thread safety. 

The `getBundleSize()` function simply returns the size of the bundle with locking mechanism for thread safety.

Finally, the `threadSafeLoadBundle()` is the wrapper for loading bundle safely in multiple threads. It accepts filename as an argument and passes it to loadBundle(). Then it calls getBundleSize() to retrieve and print size of the loaded bundle.

