Here is a sample implementation of a C# function that meets your requirements using BinaryFormatter to load and deserialize binary data from a network share. It uses a ReaderWriterLockSlim to ensure concurrency safety. It also includes error handling for common exceptions, including file not found, corrupted files and network failures.

```csharp
using System;
using System.IO;
using System.Runtime.Serialization.Formatters.Binary;
using System.Threading;

public class BinaryFileLoader<T> where T : class
{
    private ReaderWriterLockSlim _lock = new ReaderWriterLockSlim();

    public T LoadFromFile(string filePath)
    {
        if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(filePath))
            throw new ArgumentException("Invalid file path");

        try
        {
            using (_lock.Write())
            {
                BinaryFormatter formatter = new BinaryFormatter();

                using (FileStream fs = File.OpenRead(filePath))
                {
                    return (T)formatter.Deserialize(fs);
                }
            }
        }
        catch (FileNotFoundException ex)
        {
            Console.WriteLine("File not found: " + ex.Message);
        }
        catch (IOException ex)
        {
            Console.WriteLine("IO exception while reading the file: " + ex.Message);
        }
        catch (UnauthorizedAccessException ex)
        {
            Console.WriteLine("Access denied to read the file: " + ex.Message);
        }
        catch (InvalidCastException ex)
        {
            Console.WriteLine("Corrupted data in file: " + ex.Message);
        }
        catch (SerializationException ex)
        {
            Console.WriteLine("Error during deserialization: " + ex.Message);
        }
        catch (Exception ex)
        {
            Console.WriteLine("An unexpected error occurred: " + ex.Message);
        }

        return null;
    }
}
```
This class uses a `ReaderWriterLockSlim` to ensure thread safety while reading from the file and is exception safe with try-catch blocks to handle common errors including file not found, IO exceptions, unauthorized access, corrupted data and serialization errors. 

It can be used as follows:
```csharp
class Program
{
    static void Main(string[] args)
    {
        var loader = new BinaryFileLoader<YourType>();
        var result = loader.LoadFromFile("network_file_path");

        if (result != null)
            Console.WriteLine("Data loaded successfully!");
        else
            Console.WriteLine("Failed to load data.");
    }
}
```
This code can be further optimized for performance by implementing caching, where the deserialized objects are stored in memory and reused if they haven't been modified on disk since the last time they were loaded. Also, this class could be expanded to support different types of serialization methods or protocols, not just binary serialization with BinaryFormatter. 

