Here is an example of how you might implement a semaphore management system in C. For simplicity, I've used pthreads library instead of any OS-specific code. Please note that this is just a basic solution and lacks some features mentioned like logging error messages, tracking usage statistics, etc. These are important considerations to be taken into account when implementing a production ready code. 

```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <pthread.h> 
#include <semaphore.h> 

// Structure to hold semaphore data and statistics.
typedef struct {
    sem_t sem;
    int initialValue;
    pthread_mutex_t mutex;
    int acquiredCount;
    int releasedCount;
} SemaphoreData;

// Function to initialize the semaphore.
int initializeSemaphore(SemaphoreData* data, int initialValue) {
    // Initialize semaphore with the given value.
    if (sem_init(&data->sem, 0, initialValue) != 0) {
        perror("Failed to initialize semaphore");
        return -1;
    }

    data->initialValue = initialValue;
    pthread_mutex_init(&data->mutex, NULL);
    data->acquiredCount = 0;
    data->releasedCount = 0;

    return 0;
}

// Function to acquire the semaphore.
void acquireSemaphore(SemaphoreData* data) {
    // Wait on the semaphore and increment acquired count.
    sem_wait(&data->sem);
    pthread_mutex_lock(&data->mutex);
    ++data->acquiredCount;
    pthread_mutex_unlock(&data->mutex);
}

// Function to release the semaphore.
void releaseSemaphore(SemaphoreData* data) {
    // Post on the semaphore and increment released count.
    sem_post(&data->sem);
    pthread_mutex_lock(&data->mutex);
    ++data->releasedCount;
    pthread_mutex_unlock(&data->mutex);
}

// Function to delete the semaphore.
void deleteSemaphore(SemaphoreData* data) {
    // Destroy the semaphore and mutex.
    sem_destroy(&data->sem);
    pthread_mutex_destroy(&data->mutex);
}
``` 
This code is designed to be thread safe, using a mutex lock when accessing the acquisition and release counts. It's also implemented in a way that makes it easy to integrate into an existing multi-threaded application without causing deadlocks or race conditions. However, more features such as error handling, logging etc., are necessary for production code. Please note that this implementation does not handle dynamic changing of initial semaphore values. You might need to create and manage a new semaphore for each different initial value.

