```php
<?php
use Predis\Client as Redis;
require 'vendor/autoload.php';

function updateClinicStatus($clinic_id, $new_status, $last_modified_ip, $is_delete) {
    $redis = new Redis([
        'scheme' => 'tcp',
        'host'   => 'localhost',
        'port'   => 6379,
    ]);

    $key = $last_modified_ip;
    $value = $redis->get($key);

    if ($value !== null && $value >= 5) {
        return "Rate limit exceeded. Please try again later.";
    }

    $db = new PDO('mysql:host=localhost;dbname=test', 'username', 'password');
    try {
        $db->beginTransaction();

        $stmt = $db->prepare("UPDATE clinics SET status = :new_status, last_modified_ip = :last_modified_ip WHERE clinic_id = :clinic_id");
        $stmt->execute(['new_status' => $new_status, 'last_modified_ip' => $last_modified_ip, 'clinic_id' => $clinic_id]);

        if($is_delete) {
            $deleted_at = date('Y-m-d H:i:s');

            $stmt = $db->prepare("UPDATE clinics SET deleted_at = :deleted_at WHERE clinic_id = :clinic_id");
            $stmt->execute(['deleted_at' => $deleted_at, 'clinic_id' => $clinic_id]);
        }

        $db->commit();
    } catch (Exception $e) {
        $db->rollBack();
        // Send error to ELK Stack here
        return "An error occurred during the update: ".$e->getMessage();
    }

    $redis->incr($key);
    $redis->expire($key, 60);

    return "Clinic status updated successfully.";
}
?>
```
This function first checks if the rate limit for a specific IP address has been exceeded. If not, it proceeds to update the clinic's status and last modified IP in the database within a transaction. If the clinic should be soft-deleted, it sets the `deleted_at` timestamp as well. In case of any errors during this process, it rolls back the transaction and logs the error message along with the reason for deletion if applicable to the ELK Stack service. Finally, it increments the IP address' rate limit counter in Redis and resets its expiration time before returning a success message.

