Implementing such a complete IoT data processing system is beyond the scope of this platform, but here's an example to illustrate how you might start solving each of these problems in C++. This code does not include error handling or auditing for simplicity but you can add that yourself. 

```cpp
#include <fstream>
#include <limits>
#include <iostream>
#include <string>

class IOTData{
    public:
        void readAndProcess(std::ifstream& inputFile, std::ofstream& outputFile){
            double smallest = std::numeric_limits<double>::max();  // initialize to largest possible value
            double largest = std::numeric_limits<double>::lowest(); // initialize to lowest possible value

            std::string line;
            while (std::getline(inputFile, line)) {
                try{
                    double number = std::stod(line);   // convert string to double

                    if (number < smallest) 
                        smallest = number;    // update smallest number so far

                    if (number > largest)
                        largest = number;     // update largest number so far
                } catch (std::invalid_argument& e){
                    std::cout << "Invalid data format: " << line << std::endl;
                } catch (std::out_of_range& e){
                    std::cout << "Number is out of range: " << line << std::endl;
                }
            }

            outputFile << "Smallest number: " << smallest << "\nLargest number: " << largest;
        }
};

int main(){
    IOTData dataProcessor;

    try{
        std::ifstream inputFile("input.txt"); // open the file to read from

        if (!inputFile){
            throw std::runtime_error("Could not open file 'input.txt' for reading.");
        }

        std::ofstream outputFile("output.txt", std::ios::app); // append mode, open or create the file to write to
        dataProcessor.readAndProcess(inputFile, outputFile);
    } catch (std::runtime_error& e){
        std::cout << e.what() << std::endl;
    }

    return 0;
}
```

This code reads sensor data from a text file and finds the smallest and largest values in one pass through the data using an algorithm that uses O(1) space, making it quite efficient in terms of memory usage. However, this program is not designed for scalability or efficiency under varying network conditions as required. For such needs, more advanced approaches would be needed (like a distributed system where data processing can be distributed across multiple machines).

