Remember to take care of file exceptions according to your needs and also, consider that SHA-256 is a cryptographic hash function which can generate collisions (two different files generating same checksum). If you need more robust file comparison, you may want to consider other hashing algorithms or compare binary data. 

The `ExcludedExtensions` array allows you to specify file extensions that should be excluded from the comparison process. Modify this array as needed based on your specific requirements.

